{"name":"Las Palmas","hex":"#c6da36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Las Palmas","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The largest city in Gran Canaria."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Las_Palmas"}],"entries":[{"title":"Las Palmas","blocks":[{"text":"Las Palmas, officially Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, is the capital and largest city of the autonomous community of the Canary Islands in Spain. With a population of 383,516 as of 2024, it is the ninth-largest city in Spain. It is also the fifth-most populous urban area in Spain and, depending on sources, ninth or tenth most populous metropolitan area in Spain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Canteras_EM1B2907_%2840642755393%29.jpg/330px-Canteras_EM1B2907_%2840642755393%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Palmas","wikidata":"Q11974"},{"title":"Las Palmas (Congress of Deputies constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Las Palmas is one of the 52 constituencies represented in the Congress of Deputies, the lower chamber of the Spanish parliament, the Cortes Generales. The constituency currently elects eight deputies. The electoral system uses the D'Hondt method and closed-list proportional voting, with a minimum threshold of three percent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/SpanishCongressDistricts%28LasPalmas%29.png/330px-SpanishCongressDistricts%28LasPalmas%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Palmas_(Congress_of_Deputies_constituency)","wikidata":"Q6492379"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Las_Palmas_panorama.jpg/500px-Las_Palmas_panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Las_Palmas_panorama.jpg/1280